(6635756, 989753, 140026, '<td valign="top">I owe a big Thank You to the DPC community for helping me to define an ideology that can be used <br/>to win first place and ''blue ribbon'' in advanced editing. Now that I''ve cracked what the ''DPC formula'', <br/>is, my challenge has come to an end. This is nothing new, Politicians had always sought out which <br/>particular ideologies are the most effective to win votes and elect themselves into power. Except in <br/>politics you can''t "ask for your vote back" or "un-vote" if you''re later dissilusioned with the president <br/>that YOU had elected. <br/> <br/>Special Thanks also goes out to the member who posted a direct .bmp image and a method to <br/>achieve the same effect. To demonstrate that one does not even need to utilise a camera at all, is <br/>could well open the floodgates for more entries using methods like this (if not already already taken <br/>place). But more clever.<br/> <br/>As for allegations of ''plagarism'', and ''judging a photo of a photo''? Welcome to the Real World! <br/>That''s what sells Units. Example: You''ve heard Madonna''s 2005 single ''Hung Up''?  It''s mostly <br/>re-cycled Abba (1979), repeated over and over. Listen for yourself: <br/><a href="//www.youtube.com/watch?v=D1RdtUJtG8s" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.youtube.com/watch?v=D1RdtUJtG8s</a>  (listen to first 10 secs)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-01-05 13:22:06.</i></td>', 'I owe a big Thank You to the DPC community for helping me to define an ideology that can be used to win first place and ''blue ribbon'' in advanced editing. Now that I''ve cracked what the ''DPC formula'', is, my challenge has come to an end. This is nothing new, Politicians had always sought out which particular ideologies are the most effective to win votes and elect themselves into power. Except in politics you can''t "ask for your vote back" or "un-vote" if you''re later dissilusioned with the president that YOU had elected.  Special Thanks also goes out to the member who posted a direct .bmp image and a method to achieve the same effect. To demonstrate that one does not even need to utilise a camera at all, is could well open the floodgates for more entries using methods like this (if not already already taken place). But more clever. As for allegations of ''plagarism'', and ''judging a photo of a photo''? Welcome to the Real World! That''s what sells Units. Example: You''ve heard Madonna''s 2005 single ''Hung Up''?  It''s mostly re-cycled Abba (1979), repeated over and over. Listen for yourself: //www.youtube.com/watch?v=D1RdtUJtG8s  (listen to first 10 secs)', '2012-01-05 12:53:39.000000', '2012-01-05 13:22:06.000000', 0),
(6635759, 989747, 140026, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the high score, I think this deserved much higher than 6.9075. It''s probably because people the voting were distracted by a certain 7.5549 scoring ''other entry'' :-)</td>', 'Congrats on the high score, I think this deserved much higher than 6.9075. It''s probably because people the voting were distracted by a certain 7.5549 scoring ''other entry'' :-)', '2012-01-05 13:14:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(6635764, 989753, 140026, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Giles_uk:</b></div><hr/><i> original image here is my guess, mirrored. see the shadow line clipping the first barge</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Close, but no cigar :-) The Poster has some features this doesn''t have. <br/> <br/>thanks for the high vote! :-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-01-05 13:55:53.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Giles_uk: original image here is my guess, mirrored. see the shadow line clipping the first barge  Close, but no cigar :-) The Poster has some features this doesn''t have.  thanks for the high vote! :-)', '2012-01-05 13:19:53.000000', '2012-01-05 13:55:53.000000', 0),
(6635782, 989753, 140026, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SwordandScales:</b></div><hr/><i> Maybe there should be some sort of screening and license process to buy a DSLR before you unleash ridiculousness on the world of photography. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually, it''s alleged that no camera at all (let alone an SLR) was used, so such screening you proposed would be ineffective! :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by SwordandScales: Maybe there should be some sort of screening and license process to buy a DSLR before you unleash ridiculousness on the world of photography.   Actually, it''s alleged that no camera at all (let alone an SLR) was used, so such screening you proposed would be ineffective! :-)', '2012-01-05 13:58:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(6635786, 989753, 140026, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JH:</b></div><hr/><i> Faking-up a fake to fool the viewers into thinking they''re viewing a real photo of a model when in fact it''s a faked photo of someone elses photo of a real scene. Genius! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Very succinctly put! <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by JH: Faking-up a fake to fool the viewers into thinking they''re viewing a real photo of a model when in fact it''s a faked photo of someone elses photo of a real scene. Genius!   Very succinctly put! ', '2012-01-05 14:01:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(6635789, 989753, 140026, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by smardaz:</b></div><hr/><i> i almost hope it gets dq''d based soley on the self-righteous tone of the description </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''ve added some more to the description for you :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by smardaz: i almost hope it gets dq''d based soley on the self-righteous tone of the description   I''ve added some more to the description for you :-)', '2012-01-05 14:05:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(6635878, 989526, 140026, '<td valign="top">This is a great. You''ve got the blur nice overall. To ''fake'' a very narrow DOF. I would of thought this would of got a MUCH higher score than it did. <br/> <br/>IMO, could of done with more blur to background behind digger, very tight up close to above digger''s cab and around arm, to make the digger stand out more. Also, I would of tried bringing downwards a full width of blur, a bit closer to the digger ,even engulfing the two men in the middle, so they look like they were outside of the faked narrow DOF.<br/> <br/>Good work!<br/> <br/></td>', 'This is a great. You''ve got the blur nice overall. To ''fake'' a very narrow DOF. I would of thought this would of got a MUCH higher score than it did.  IMO, could of done with more blur to background behind digger, very tight up close to above digger''s cab and around arm, to make the digger stand out more. Also, I would of tried bringing downwards a full width of blur, a bit closer to the digger ,even engulfing the two men in the middle, so they look like they were outside of the faked narrow DOF. Good work! ', '2012-01-05 15:03:46.000000', NULL, 0),
