(6639805, 989869, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>First impression: Stripey! And seems that I like lensbaby shots, with the fg slightly oof and the bg in focus.<br/> <br/>Artistic: I think you''ve done a good job with the patterns of light and on the walls, all leading to the cyclist in a striped shirt - accidental?  Or someone you got to wear a stripey shirt?  Either way, very good capture imho.  Perhaps a tad more overexposure, then you could have added more black and contrast to make the patterns pop a little more.  The tilt-shift effect isn''t really there, but the effect can be done in most pp programs.<br/> <br/>Technical:  The lighting is supplied by the tunnel''s fluourescents, so not too much you can do but adjust and go with it.  In tricky lighting situations it''s perfectly OK to go to Auto WB.  You should also be able to shoot in b/w (look for the word monochrome in the shooting menu).<br/> <br/>Overall: A little more contrast and possibly b/w rendering may have helped this image pop a bit more and given you a higher score.  But overall, a good attempt.  Don''t get discouraged by the low scores, btw; see them as a learning curve.  For some, DPC is almost like a gym for the photographer, providing an array of ways to help you explore and improve your photography.  Keep shooting and keep entering! :-)<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions.<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! First impression: Stripey! And seems that I like lensbaby shots, with the fg slightly oof and the bg in focus. Artistic: I think you''ve done a good job with the patterns of light and on the walls, all leading to the cyclist in a striped shirt - accidental?  Or someone you got to wear a stripey shirt?  Either way, very good capture imho.  Perhaps a tad more overexposure, then you could have added more black and contrast to make the patterns pop a little more.  The tilt-shift effect isn''t really there, but the effect can be done in most pp programs. Technical:  The lighting is supplied by the tunnel''s fluourescents, so not too much you can do but adjust and go with it.  In tricky lighting situations it''s perfectly OK to go to Auto WB.  You should also be able to shoot in b/w (look for the word monochrome in the shooting menu). Overall: A little more contrast and possibly b/w rendering may have helped this image pop a bit more and given you a higher score.  But overall, a good attempt.  Don''t get discouraged by the low scores, btw; see them as a learning curve.  For some, DPC is almost like a gym for the photographer, providing an array of ways to help you explore and improve your photography.  Keep shooting and keep entering! :-) Feel free to PM me with any questions. Susan', '2012-01-09 10:17:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(6640047, 989823, 44765, '<td valign="top">How Amazing is that? Less than 10 challenges and you are already on the first page with a star!<br/> <br/></td>', 'How Amazing is that? Less than 10 challenges and you are already on the first page with a star! ', '2012-01-09 12:55:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(6640252, 989526, 106806, '<td valign="top">What would this photo look like if we didn''t have toys and models? .... guess I''ll never know but it looks dang good.</td>', 'What would this photo look like if we didn''t have toys and models? .... guess I''ll never know but it looks dang good.', '2012-01-09 17:59:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(6641032, 989562, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>First impression: Does indeed look like a Lego car factory!  All the cranes, the buildings etc do indeed like tiny.  Quite impressive<br/> <br/>Artistic: Colourful and eye-catching, great use of the T/S effect.<br/> <br/>Technical: Good lighting, comp a little centred but understandable considering the point you wanted to make and the sheer size of the complex.  The only thing I''d possibly like to change is a slight more of a fade-out effect, you can see where the T/S ends a little too much in the bg.  But that''s fairly minor.  Your settings are perfectly fine for a handheld shot on a sunny day.<br/> <br/>Overall: Great concept and very good execution.  Glad to see you finished just below 6 with this image.  Keep up the good work and keep shooting!<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me.<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! First impression: Does indeed look like a Lego car factory!  All the cranes, the buildings etc do indeed like tiny.  Quite impressive Artistic: Colourful and eye-catching, great use of the T/S effect. Technical: Good lighting, comp a little centred but understandable considering the point you wanted to make and the sheer size of the complex.  The only thing I''d possibly like to change is a slight more of a fade-out effect, you can see where the T/S ends a little too much in the bg.  But that''s fairly minor.  Your settings are perfectly fine for a handheld shot on a sunny day. Overall: Great concept and very good execution.  Glad to see you finished just below 6 with this image.  Keep up the good work and keep shooting! Feel free to PM me. Susan', '2012-01-10 13:07:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(6641166, 989878, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>First impression: ''Aha another Posty lensbaby shot''...and I was right :-)<br/> <br/>Artistic: Intriguing find in terms of the tree and rock, amd good treatment to give it a little of posty spin. <br/> <br/>Technical: A bit dark but that adds to the mood.  Comp ok but centred.  I''m hard-pressed to see much T/S going on, though.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me.<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! First impression: ''Aha another Posty lensbaby shot''...and I was right :-) Artistic: Intriguing find in terms of the tree and rock, amd good treatment to give it a little of posty spin.  Technical: A bit dark but that adds to the mood.  Comp ok but centred.  I''m hard-pressed to see much T/S going on, though. Feel free to PM me. Susan', '2012-01-10 17:37:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(6641179, 989861, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>First Impression: Very good use of the T/S effect, and I am fond of extreme POVs like this.<br/> <br/>Artistic: Great place to shoot for this challenge, as you already have a bit of a 3/4 overhead perspective to help you out.  That, and the bright colours of the clothing against the ice, add interest and depth and movement to the shot.<br/> <br/>Technical:  Decent lighting, composition is good considering the angle.  Wondering if a little more of a zoom-in might help isolate your subject a bit more.  Would like to see some dodging used in fg just to balance out the scene, it looks a little too undefined.  But then it does work with the fadeout effect.<br/> <br/>Overall: A good solid entry that does a fine job of meeting the challenge.  It just needs a little more pop to it to give it that extra <i>je ne sais quoi</i>.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me.<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! First Impression: Very good use of the T/S effect, and I am fond of extreme POVs like this. Artistic: Great place to shoot for this challenge, as you already have a bit of a 3/4 overhead perspective to help you out.  That, and the bright colours of the clothing against the ice, add interest and depth and movement to the shot. Technical:  Decent lighting, composition is good considering the angle.  Wondering if a little more of a zoom-in might help isolate your subject a bit more.  Would like to see some dodging used in fg just to balance out the scene, it looks a little too undefined.  But then it does work with the fadeout effect. Overall: A good solid entry that does a fine job of meeting the challenge.  It just needs a little more pop to it to give it that extra je ne sais quoi. Feel free to PM me. Susan', '2012-01-10 17:44:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(6646600, 989603, 24454, '<td valign="top">Wow!  Awesome, Brian!  I am so HAPPY to see that you are able to get out and take pictures!  It looks like you''re doing juuuust great  :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Wow!  Awesome, Brian!  I am so HAPPY to see that you are able to get out and take pictures!  It looks like you''re doing juuuust great  :) ', '2012-01-16 11:36:48.000000', NULL, 0),
